===Alternative forms===
* {{q|internet slang|childish|jocular}} {{alt|en|snek}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)neg-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|snake}}, from {{inh|en|ang|snaca||snake, serpent, reptile}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*snakō|t=snake}} (compare {{cog|nds-de|Snake}}, {{m|nds-de|Snaak||snake}}, dialectal {{cog|de|Schnake||adder}}, {{cog|sv|snok||grass snake}}, {{cog|da|snog||grass snake}}, Icelandic {{m|is|snákur||snake}}), derived via {{inh|en|gem-pro|*snakô}} from {{der|en|gem-pro|*snakaną||to crawl}} (compare {{cog|goh|snahhan}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)neg-||to crawl; a creeping thing}}. Cognate with {{cog|sa|नाग|tr=nāgá||snake}}). {{doublet|en|nāga}}.

