===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2102}}A [[legless]] [[reptile]] in the order {{taxfmt|Squamata|order}} with a long, thin body and a fork-shaped tongue.
#: {{syn|en|joe blake|serpent}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1892|author=w:Oscar Wilde|title=w:A House of Pomegranates|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=6sUVAAAAYAAJ|passage=The man writhed like a trampled '''snake''', and a red foam bubbled from his lips.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=April|author=Timothy H. Cobb|title=The Kenya-Uganda Railway|journal=Railway Magazine|page=263|text=After dark the train is a lighted '''snake''', as, even when the passengers' lights are out, each carriage has a side-light in the middle just under the eaves.}}
# A [[treacherous]] person; a [[rat]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1838|author=w:Charles Dickens|title=w:Nicholas Nickleby|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=rLs0AAAAMAAJ|passage=Mrs. Kenwigs was horror-stricken to think that she should ever have nourished in her bosom such a '''snake''', adder, viper, serpent, and base crocodile, as Henrietta Petowker.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2021|author=Peter McKenna|title={{w|Kin (Irish TV series)|Kin}}|season=1|number=2|time=5:51|role=Frank Kinsella|actor=w:Aidan Gillen|passage=Well, if it was Moore, he's a fucking '''snake'''.}}
# A person who acts deceitfully for social gain.
# A [[tool]] for unclogging [[plumbing]].
#: {{syn|en|auger|plumber's snake}}
# A tool to aid [[cable]] pulling.
#: {{syn|en|wirepuller}}
# {{lb|en|UK|Australia}} A flavoured [[jube]] ([[confectionary]]) in the shape of a snake.
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[trouser snake|Trouser snake]]; the [[penis]].
#: {{syn|en|trouser snake}}
# {{lb|en|maths}} A series of [[Bézier curve]]s.
# {{lb|en|cartomancy}} The seventh [[Lenormand]] card.
# {{lb|en|MLE|MTE}} An [[informer]]; a [[rat]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:informant}}
#: {{ux|en|Gem’s a '''snake''' for Kamale, man.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2017-04-07|title=War Dub|artist=Little T (Josh Tate)|text=Yo, bare people and the '''snakes''', yeah, they're just grass / Next minute you're the mate, yeah / Next day stab in the back}}
# {{lb|en|finance|historical}} {{short for|en|snake in the tunnel}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2001|author=W. Bonefeld|title=The Politics of Europe: Monetary Union and Class|page=69
|passage=The '''snake''' failed to provide an anchor for currency stability and, through it, disinflation.}}
# {{short for|en|black snake||firework that creates a trail of ash}}

